Centralized Logging – One Place for All Your Logs 📜

🔹 What is Centralized Logging?
Centralized logging is the practice of collecting logs from multiple servers, applications, and containers into a single location for easier monitoring and troubleshooting.
Instead of checking logs on each server individually, engineers can view everything from one platform.

❓ Why Centralize Logs?
In production environments, applications run across multiple servers and containers.
Without centralized logging:
❌ Logs are scattered across systems
 ❌ Troubleshooting takes longer
 ❌ Difficult to correlate events

With centralized logging:
✔ One place for all logs 📦
 ✔ Faster debugging 🚀
 ✔ Easy search and filtering 🔍
 ✔ Better monitoring and security 🔒

