 ⬇️
 Visualization Dashboard 📊
This architecture helps teams quickly search and analyze logs from all systems.

💡 Real-world Example
A microservices application runs on 10 Kubernetes pods.
One service starts failing.
Without centralized logging, engineers check logs on each pod manually. ❌
With centralized logging, they search for "ERROR" in one dashboard and instantly find the failing service. ✅

🧠 Key Takeaways
✔ Centralized logging stores logs in one place 📦
 ✔ Simplifies troubleshooting 🔍
 ✔ Speeds up incident resolution 🚀
 ✔ Essential for production and microservices ☸️
